[{:db/id "q-162583/selection/f5e27680dccf325a2e1eff7c59a550bc6faa6324173f4446d6066305db5e7c5a" :answer/id #uuid "73dcd527-2255-580c-a940-74ec402491b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-y-2z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162583/selection/d883a6d355136141c5b13cb2651adf99d05e1490ef67e5d137cea50bb4338635" :answer/id #uuid "cb234d0c-4336-51b2-b53e-3886cee8f26a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x+4z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162583/selection/6cfbbb056524e6ddc9cd35a423174595bb966a12ed61e5437d7b89b001228730" :answer/id #uuid "eed5b62a-cd47-5498-93ea-5748a0cdf7bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+3z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162583/selection/94f570e3e356d78a1e722a70592be36f821bcd6c36c39f2acb0c19fe88a7865f" :answer/id #uuid "1b9753ae-72b5-58ce-8026-675977769eed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x-z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162583/selection/823e0b5d952e18913c8ca09efd5d6bebaed6397015c00aa11ecfbc771e3dfe40" :answer/id #uuid "ab811755-3b35-502e-bee8-a0c3d59acbfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-z+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162583/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "614dbe19-4218-5e05-8664-99c4d9231395" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162583/selection/94f570e3e356d78a1e722a70592be36f821bcd6c36c39f2acb0c19fe88a7865f" :answer-field/choices ["q-162583/selection/f5e27680dccf325a2e1eff7c59a550bc6faa6324173f4446d6066305db5e7c5a" "q-162583/selection/d883a6d355136141c5b13cb2651adf99d05e1490ef67e5d137cea50bb4338635" "q-162583/selection/6cfbbb056524e6ddc9cd35a423174595bb966a12ed61e5437d7b89b001228730" "q-162583/selection/94f570e3e356d78a1e722a70592be36f821bcd6c36c39f2acb0c19fe88a7865f" "q-162583/selection/823e0b5d952e18913c8ca09efd5d6bebaed6397015c00aa11ecfbc771e3dfe40"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162583" :question/id #uuid "20faa8ac-7475-55a0-94fb-35eb1571259e" :question/math-academy-id "q-162583" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=0,$ $x=4,$ $y=-1,$ $y=1,$ $z=0,$ $z=2.$ Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=({x}^{2}+y)\\,i-yz\\,j+4xz\\,k,$ the flux of $F$ across $S$ can be written as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing part of the expression?" :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-yz)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4xz) \\\\  & =2x-z+4x \\\\  & =6x-z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}(6x-z)\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,6x-z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-162583/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a3fd63f-9991-5781-b4f8-9c4b0abc65ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162583"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162589/selection/969f97a353343dbcdc584f9128f5b43258e96240c1288170ca4390f7c96012a5" :answer/id #uuid "813ac4a4-e0e0-552e-822d-24a6ad256672" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}^{2}\\,3{y}^{2}+xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162589/selection/207051e6a46812b7870cdc8d851dba9066c56f838c71dccc58f23b6c1c831225" :answer/id #uuid "9eff9ad9-d3a6-5a6f-9f24-bbd6e67b2971" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,2xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162589/selection/3c4b05aff60db0342dde672e3d8466e0929210057fce1e920c08a9ce62f8e774" :answer/id #uuid "82519da3-22f7-5b2a-b72f-b730c0825fd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}^{2}\\,2xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162589/selection/14d412ae1b37374fccfbf2374bca18067dbadec64f3d0bfbe2a949c85a5cc39b" :answer/id #uuid "04ca41fa-fa6e-5e8e-89da-66fc415279f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2}^{{z}^{2}+{x}^{2}}\\,3{y}^{2}+xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162589/selection/a36b01f76222603e212d6a1d725d572946bc8d217343a3874a7aefe8b3f820fd" :answer/id #uuid "72dc0460-a429-54c0-9129-56040ffb9907" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,x+y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162589/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "88d3b66b-ebc2-5e30-af7c-cde4cb13f65f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162589/selection/3c4b05aff60db0342dde672e3d8466e0929210057fce1e920c08a9ce62f8e774" :answer-field/choices ["q-162589/selection/969f97a353343dbcdc584f9128f5b43258e96240c1288170ca4390f7c96012a5" "q-162589/selection/207051e6a46812b7870cdc8d851dba9066c56f838c71dccc58f23b6c1c831225" "q-162589/selection/3c4b05aff60db0342dde672e3d8466e0929210057fce1e920c08a9ce62f8e774" "q-162589/selection/14d412ae1b37374fccfbf2374bca18067dbadec64f3d0bfbe2a949c85a5cc39b" "q-162589/selection/a36b01f76222603e212d6a1d725d572946bc8d217343a3874a7aefe8b3f820fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162589" :question/id #uuid "838b34a2-ad5a-5f20-9f09-00b68f844e2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-162589" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the boundary of the finite solid region enclosed by the planes $x=-1,$ $x=1,$ $z=0,$ $z=1,$ and the surfaces $y={x}^{2}+{z}^{2}$ and $y=2.$ Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=({y}^{3}-z)\\,i+z\\,j+2xyz\\,k,$ the flux of $F$ across $S$ can be written as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{3}-z)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2xyz) \\\\  & =0+0+2xy \\\\  & =2xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}2xy\\,\\text{d}V,\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is a type III solid region that can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}2xy\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}^{2}\\,2xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162589/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a3fd63f-9991-5781-b4f8-9c4b0abc65ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162589"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162581/selection/48926eb34f1e846b681031fafa97063badde87056b576f4fc700078200d4dc3e" :answer/id #uuid "a12d3323-b03b-516d-94a9-8b30a8375979" :answer/type :an